;
; How Furrow files one cell in MYRA (furrow_rules.h FW4): a sparse record,
; kept only for a cell that holds something, under the sheet's number, the
; row and the column, with its kind (1 a number, 2 money in minor units,
; 3 a formula) and its value. Furrow asks whether the numbers fit before
; it keeps them.
^ZXFURROW(sheet:i4, row:i7, col:i5) = kind:i1! ^ value:i18!
